codex
The source uses several responses to unpredictable cases: it preserves some existing results, rejects some optimizations, and raises guest exceptions elsewhere. I’m tracing decode rejection to distinguish declining read-ahead from stopping execution. There’s also a count correction: 496 BFI field pairs have `width <= 0`; 465 are negative and 31 are zero.

