The closest comparison is MIPS `X(ins)`: its shift count simplifies to `31 - msb`, stays in range, and produces a zero mask when `msb < pos`, preserving the destination’s low 32 bits. That supports no-op behavior by analogy. ARM also has exception and halt paths, so the tree does not establish one universal policy for unpredictable BFI widths.

